# Text files are checked out with LF line endings on every system, so a Windows checkout reads
# and builds the same bytes as macOS and Linux (git's Windows default would rewrite them CRLF).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows starter keeps CRLF line endings byte for byte (the batch-file convention);
# never let git rewrite them on checkout, in the index, or in the GitHub ZIP.
*.bat -text
